    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c02-0102",
      "sentenceId": "c02-s05-p025-06405-s003",
      "sentenceText": "In Thus Spoke Zarathustra he describes the temptation to lead a happy and virtuous life as follows: “They would laud and lure me into a small virtue; they would persuade my foot to the ticktock of a small happiness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a6cf0a1bcedfe45e7e5f5d59f9778bd9c8a58d5a77c82f32d797a9fab2cc5fef",
      "readingUnitId": "c02-s05-p025-06405-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c02-081",
      "parentFingerprint": "caea59f95e5f60b9fd7714c5bbbb552b55f19b10743ca09297e21e8b5d2e43aa",
      "passageSha256": "3a52a31f1c72997dcc3d5228914d45a6abff5a0b02ecda752e08a5fbedb852cb",
      "pdfPages": [
        25,
        26
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c02-0103",
      "sentenceId": "c02-s05-p025-06405-s004",
      "sentenceText": "I walk among this people and I keep my eyes open: they have become smaller, and they are becoming smaller and smaller; but this is due to their doctrine of happiness and virtue.",
      "sentenceSha256": "ab6cf3847dbf14158a14a21a55733f8bc6f7e2bd0491ba09142ce72fd7beafd3",
      "readingUnitId": "c02-s05-p025-06405-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c02-082",
      "parentFingerprint": "0dc727fa1f4143939eda955b4b6fc5eb71bbd5d432f47c0a5c5700581e8a44d8",
      "passageSha256": "dd7a8ef22e65cb271664fe53c315f4529d5c0dc62a60b163bf1e13801c8d9ab0",
      "pdfPages": [
        26
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c02-0104",
      "sentenceId": "c02-s05-p025-06405-s007",
      "sentenceText": "Modestly to embrace a small happiness—that they call ‘resignation’—and modestly they squint the whole for another small happiness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "1c46301f0483e9e5f2cd705696528c2cfc901b3e3f5129cdbdb3529149d6c152",
      "readingUnitId": "c02-s05-p025-06405-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c02-082",
      "parentFingerprint": "0dc727fa1f4143939eda955b4b6fc5eb71bbd5d432f47c0a5c5700581e8a44d8",
